{
	title: 'Edit the last prompt while the model works',
	spec: 'Port the old Hal feature the user relies on daily (tasks/j1/states.md, Editing the last prompt; artifacts: the old client and host code). Up arrow on an empty prompt while the session works pauses it and loads the last prompt into the editor. Sending the edit: if nothing happened since that prompt, or only read-only tools, the edited prompt replaces the old one and the turn runs again as if it had been written that way; if tools with side effects ran, history stays and the edit is sent on top. Down with unchanged text, or Escape, continues the paused turn. History is append-only in hal2: replacing a prompt is a new record that supersedes the old prompt and its turn for the provider, not a rewrite of the file. Both clients get it; the decision of which case applies is made by the host from history, not by each client.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['2r'],
	notes: [
		'Durable form: a `user` record with `replaces: true` supersedes the last prompt record (replay.lastPrompt: a user record with text) and every record after it, inbox records excepted. replay.current(records) applies that; toMessages and transcript.fromSnapshot read through it, while states, inbox.pending and recoveries read raw records.',
		"Protocol: submit.amend (boolean). host.amend replaces when the session is not busy and every tool call since the prompt is tools.readOnly (Tool.readOnly; only `read` now, unknown tools count as side effects); otherwise it is host.submit. Only the prompt's last text is edited: texts it delivered from the inbox before that are kept in the replacing record. Clients hear a `prompt` event with `replaces`, then a turn-start without prompt.",
		"Race: the client sends pause then submit amend back to back, so the paused runTurn is still unwinding. host.act defers an amend on a paused session while host.state.running has the id until Running.done (runTurn's promise) settles, so the paused turn end lands before the edit.",
		"Transcript.prompt is the item index where the last prompt's items start; a `prompt` event with `replaces` cuts items there.",
		"Clients share src/common/amend.ts: begin (Up on an empty prompt while states.busy: pause + load the last prompt item), enter (submit amend; Alt-Enter queues and an emptied edit continues as usual), resume (Down unchanged or Escape: continue if paused or the pause is in flight). Escape keeps changed text in the editor; nothing typed is dropped. The old Hal's '/rebase' and side-effect copy modes are not ported: the host decides.",
		"With drafts (rw) the edit is a draft like any text: Up puts the old prompt in the draft, and the edit goes out through drafts.submit(id, text, queue, amend), so an unacknowledged edit is resent as an edit (Sending.amend). With forms (w4) an open question takes keys before the edit keys; replay.current keeps answer records, as a question may predate the prompt."
	]
}
